Please map these incoming records for sports and entertainment crew dispatch in Guatemala, Central America.

Event dispatch: copy booking_key; trim event_reference; classify null or empty as MISSING, a whole-string mismatch to GT[0-9]{6} as INVALID, otherwise VALID. Output that classification as reference_state and the trimmed uppercase text as canonical_reference. Validation uses the trimmed text before uppercasing. Output dispatch_blocked as lock_active, treating null as false.

Count one issue each for:
- reference_state other than VALID;
- crew_needed null or nonpositive;
- crew_available null, negative, or less than crew_needed (compare the two fields only when crew_needed is nonnull);
- venue_label null or blank after trimming;
- dispatcher_tag not matching the exact whole-string pattern DC[0-9]{3}, including null;
- lock_active being true.

Output the count as issue_total. Set dispatch_lane to REVIEW if any issue exists; otherwise RESERVE if crew_available exceeds crew_needed, or READY if they are equal.

Set staffing_size to UNKNOWN for null crew_needed, INVALID at <=0, LARGE at >=40, SMALL otherwise. Set coverage_level to UNKNOWN if either crew count is null; otherwise INVALID if crew_needed <=0 or crew_available <0; otherwise SHORT if crew_available < crew_needed, EXACT if equal, or SURPLUS if greater. venue_ready means venue_label is nonblank after trimming; dispatcher_verified uses the exact whole-string DC pattern without trimming.

